SurfCPU contract patch for Spike (riscv-isa-sim) at commit 5a760667bf0d0ab893173b9eeff9c109c8d7dd9a
File: surfcpu-contract.patch Date: 10/15/26 (SurfCPU)

Spike is the reference model for SurfCPU's verification (docs/VERIFICATION.md). Where the
RISC-V specification leaves a choice to the implementation (WARL/WLRL fields, the ID CSRs,
whether unimplemented-PMP and trigger CSRs exist), docs/ISA.md fixes SurfCPU's choice and
this patch makes Spike make the same one, so a comparison never fails on a choice the
contract allows. Nothing else changes: instruction semantics, traps and every other CSR
are Spike's. Applied by sim/ref/spike/build-spike.sh (git apply).

  * marchid reads 0 and mimpid 0x00000100 (SURF_SOC_VERSION), as ISA.md section 2.
  * With --pmpregions=0, pmpcfg0-15 and pmpaddr0-63 exist and read as zero; writes are
    ignored (stock Spike makes them illegal).
  * With --triggers=0, tselect, tdata1-3, tinfo and mcontext do not exist (stock Spike
    keeps tselect and read-only-zero tdata/tinfo and a writable mcontext).
  * misa ignores writes (stock Spike lets software clear M, A, F, D, C, ...).
  * mtvec.MODE is fixed at 0 (stock Spike keeps vectored mode).
  * mcountinhibit keeps only CY and IR (stock Spike also has the HPM bits with Zihpm).
  * mcause keeps bit 31 and bits 4:0 (stock Spike keeps every bit).

